ASSIGNMENT 6

Instructions for Students
● Create a separate HTML and CSS file for each question.
● Do not use JavaScript or any external CSS frameworks.
● You may use semantic HTML5 tags (header, main, section, footer, etc.).
● All designs should be responsive and use only Flexbox or Grid for layout.

1. Create a personal portfolio webpage layout using Flexbox.
Requirements:
● Header: includes your name (left) and navigation links (right).
● Main area: two sections — an “About Me” section (text) and an image section.
● Footer: simple copyright text centered.
● Use display: flex; to align header items horizontally and main content side-by-side.
● Ensure that when the screen width is below 700px, all sections stack vertically.
● Center items both vertically and horizontally using align-items and
justify-content.

2. Design a 4-column product gallery using CSS Grid.
Requirements:
● Create a grid of 8 product cards.
● Each card should contain a product name and price.
● Use grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); for desktop.
● Adjust to 2 columns on tablets and 1 column on mobile using media queries.
● Add hover effects on each card: use transform: scale(1.05) and transition:
0.3s.

● Cards should have equal height regardless of content length.

3. Create a 3-section homepage using Flexbox: Header, Main, and Footer.
Requirements:
● Header: navigation links spaced evenly using justify-content: space-around;.
● Main: three boxes (Services, Projects, Contact) horizontally aligned.
● On hover, each box should slightly rotate (transform: rotate(2deg);).
● Footer: stays at the bottom and spans full width.
● The layout must remain balanced at all screen sizes.

4. Build a dashboard layout using CSS Grid.
Requirements:
● Header spans the top across all columns.
● Sidebar on the left with vertical navigation.
● Main content with 4 boxes arranged in 2 rows and 2 columns.
● One box should span two columns (grid-column: span 2;).
● Use grid-gap for spacing and fractional units (fr) for widths.
● Add hover effects that scale up the box and cast a shadow.

5. Design a pricing section using Flexbox.
Requirements:
● Create three pricing cards aligned horizontally.
● The middle card should be slightly larger and highlighted with a different background
color.
● On hover, cards should rise up slightly (transform: translateY(-10px)), with a
smooth transition.

● Add a simple fade-in animation for all three cards when the page loads using
@keyframes.
● Make the layout stack vertically below 750px.

6. Create a responsive blog layout using CSS Grid.
Requirements:
● Header with title and nav links.
● Sidebar on the left containing categories.
● Main content area displaying two blog posts side-by-side.
● Footer with contact info.
● Use grid-template-areas to structure the layout.
● Below 800px, sidebar should move below the main content.
● Add padding, margins, and equal spacing using gap.

7. Design a CSS loading animation using only div elements.
Requirements:
● Create three small circles that move up and down repeatedly.
● Use @keyframes to control the motion and timing.
● Each circle should start its animation with a slight delay.
● Center the animation on the page using Flexbox alignment.
● Use transform: translateY() and animation-iteration-count:
infinite;.

8. Build a photo gallery using Grid with hover transformations.
Requirements:
● Use grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));.

● Each image should fill its grid cell completely and scale up slightly on hover.
● Add transition: transform 0.5s ease; for smooth zoom effect.
● Include image captions below each image using <figcaption>.
● Layout should automatically adjust to screen size.

9. Create a card flip animation using CSS Transformations and Transitions.
Requirements:
● Build one card that flips 180 degrees on hover.
● Front side: shows title and image.
● Back side: shows text description.
● Use transform-style: preserve-3d; and perspective: 1000px;.
● Implement the flip using transform: rotateY(180deg); and smooth transitions.
● Card must remain centered on screen using Flexbox.

10. Design a responsive webpage layout combining Flexbox and Grid.
Requirements:
● Header with logo and nav links using Flexbox.
● Main area divided into a 2-column Grid (Article + Sidebar).
● Footer spans the full width with centered text.
● Inside the main article, include three boxes aligned using Flexbox.
● Use @keyframes to animate one element (e.g., a title fades in or moves up).
● Ensure the layout collapses into a single column on mobile screens.